Execute the firmware SPURS job-queue port path used for secondary-bone
physics. The previously unresolved create, port-copy-push and sync imports
returned success without running the queued jobs, leaving identity output
matrices for the subsequent world-to-model transform. Queue/port records own
copied guest descriptors and dispatch registered jobs in submission order;
missing images and staging failures remain visible through error/sync/join.
Use firmware job error codes and four-byte guest error-cause pointers.

Provide the per-job manager control block required by the queue job CRT,
rather than only the JobContext2 argument used by the existing chain path.
Preserve negative staging results
through the fingerprint dispatcher. The legacy compact queue API remains a
separate compatibility shim.

